File Index

/affect-echo.plugin.ts
Purpose: Echoes affect gains and losses to the terminal with configurable colors.

/brew.plugin.ts
Purpose: This plugin enables users to define and execute custom item brewing recipes with letter mappings, symbol shortcuts, and persistent storage.

/colorkit.plugin.ts
Purpose: Colorize log lines based on configurable rules without trigger scripts.

/combat-compression.plugin.ts
Purpose: Squelches selected combat-log line classes (Damage/Avoidance/Condition/Death/Flee/Rescue/Disarm/Ambient/Item Use/Status/Incapacitation/Attack Flavor/UI Noise) via patterns verified against the real server log corpus (incl. Coliseum- and Bloodbath-arena mining passes); exports PATTERNS and the damage-verb DAMAGE_LINE_PATTERN for reuse (e.g. text-to-speech's combat compression and Arena Observer Mode).

/disarm.plugin.ts
Purpose: Automatically re-wields disarmed weapons by mapping item names to aliases.

/enchant.plugin.ts
Purpose: Enchant Helper plugin automates item enchanting with configurable item lists and spell casting.

/gourd.plugin.ts
Purpose: Tracks and manages potion gourd inventory with scan, quaff, and drop commands.

/highlighter.plugin.ts
Purpose: Highlights player names in chat logs by organization color based on configurable regex rules.

/people.plugin.ts
Purpose: Parses player data from game commands into a shared database for tracking and annotation.

/peopleDb.ts
Purpose: Manages persistent storage and retrieval of character data for the game client.

/questbot-stats-idb.ts
Purpose: IndexedDB storage for QuestBot statistics with running aggregates and session management.

/questbot.plugin.ts
Purpose: Automates DSL questing cycles with stats tracking and command interfaces.

/respell.plugin.ts
Purpose: Automatically recasts spells when they drop based on user-defined mappings.

/roller.plugin.ts
Purpose: Automatically accepts or rejects stat rolls based on configurable thresholds and prompts.

/speech-text.ts
Purpose: Sanitizes text bound for a speech engine — strips the full escape-sequence set (any CSI final byte, private-mode toggles, OSC strings, a sequence cut off by a chunk boundary, stray control bytes), not just the SGR colors the other stripAnsi helpers remove, so the synthesizer never reads codes aloud.

/standup.plugin.ts
Purpose: Enables automatic standing up in game when specific knockdown phrases are detected.

/text-to-speech.plugin.ts
Purpose: Reads text aloud via browser speechSynthesis — auto-reads the play area (filtered, capped, respects line-squelch, auto-skips PROMPT/status lines via a vitals-shape heuristic since format is per-player, groups bursts within a debounced window into one utterance joined by spaces so word-wrap doesn't add pauses) and/or an on-demand floating button that reads selected/focused page text; also optional spoken alerts on self/enemy health-tier changes (GMCP-driven, deduped), on game:tick (with the in-game time from that same event), and on self-stun (reuses Stun Highlight's text matchers — CharData.stance in types-global is NOT a position/incapacitation flag, it's the offensive/normal/defensive combat-stance toggle, so it's not a usable stun signal; when Combat Mode is Battle Focus this same toggle also drives self-debuff callouts from game:affect-added/removed, using the modifier's sign — inverted for ac — to tell debuff from buff, skipping zero-modifier binary effects like stuns/charms). Combat Mode ('off' | 'battleFocus'): Battle Focus is a "game caster" mode for the player's own fights sharing speakArenaLineIfWorthy's classify-and-speak pipeline with Arena Observer Mode below (squelches Damage/Avoidance/Ambient/Item Use/Attack Flavor/UI Noise/weapon-flag procs, speaks Status/Incapacitation/Disarm/Death/Flee immediately, dedupes repeats by canonicalized shape) but with condition-tier lines dropped rather than spoken (that's the self/enemy health-alert toggles' job, avoiding a double announcement) and chat lines left alone (this is the player's own conversation, not spectator noise). Also Arena Observer Mode, a "game caster" mode covering BOTH DSL arena types via one self-contained pipeline (bypasses the normal squelch/prompt/Combat-Mode/include-exclude chain entirely): Coliseum is spectator-only, gated per-line on the five Coliseum rooms' broadcast prefix (no "you" tracking); Bloodbath is participant-driven, gated on the player's current room (tracked off the vitals-prompt line, which also closes a room-look-render squelch block opened by the Exits line), with "Bloodbath System:" announcements always speaking regardless of room and the repeating "You sure are BLEEDING!" nag deduped to one mention. Both arena paths ALSO drop chat/speech lines entirely (via strict-chat-classifier.ts's classifyStrictChatSubtype — say/tell/yell/gossip/OOC/etc.), unlike Battle Focus mode which leaves them alone — built from Coliseum (room names via C:\Projects\DSL\AGL\Text\2024-02-17_Piknim_Pardo.txt) and Bloodbath (room mechanics via C:\Projects\DSL\GameLogs\GameLog-DSL_2023-11-10-Fri.txt) log corpus mining passes. Speech pipeline: include/exclude patterns are regex-capable (literal-substring fallback on invalid syntax); utterance-start delay (default 150ms) + a resume()/cancel() nudge plus a near-silent primer utterance queued immediately ahead of each real one, absorbing Chrome/Edge's start-of-buffer clip (reported to still cut into the first word even without a prior utterance or idle period) instead of the real utterance eating it.

/voice-dictation.plugin.ts
Purpose: Speech-to-text dictation (merged 2026-07-21 from the former voice-dictation-engine + voice-dictation-input pair into one config flow) — chooses the recognition engine (browser Web Speech API vs. downloadable wav2vec2, literal/non-generative), language, model, and custom vocabulary, then dictates into either the command input (reclaims the hidden mic slot in CommandInput.tsx via an inline display-style override, not injected CSS) or any other focused page text field. usePlugins.ts migrates existing installs of the old two plugin ids into this one on load.

/warlock-alphabet.plugin.ts
Purpose: This plugin helps warlocks manage spell recipes by tracking item assignments to brew letters and automating correct insertion order.

/weapon-flag-squelch.plugin.ts
Purpose: Squelches weapon-flag proc echo lines (Frost/Flaming/Shocking/Vampiric/Stunning/Mana Drain/Holy/Unholy/Poison) via patterns verified against the real server log corpus; exports PATTERNS for reuse (e.g. text-to-speech's combat compression).
